jsonkit mcp · Serve this application's tools to an MCP client, over stdin and stdout or, with --http, over HTTP.

USAGE
  jsonkit mcp [options]
  jsonkit mcp <command> [options]

COMMANDS
  install    Register this application's MCP server with your coding agents.
  uninstall  Remove this application's MCP server from your coding agents.
  config     Print a client configuration that starts this application's MCP server.

OPTIONS
      --http <http>  Serve over HTTP at this address instead of stdin and stdout: a port, or host:port. A port alone listens on 127.0.0.1, and port 0 takes any free port.

GLOBAL OPTIONS
  -h, --help        Show this help.
  -V, --version     Print the version.
  -M, --manifest    Print this command's manifest as JSON.
  -e, --explain     Explain the selected command and exit.
      --[no-]color  Turn color on or off, overriding NO_COLOR.
  -v, --verbose...  Show more detail. Repeat it for more.
  -q, --quiet       Hide info and success messages.

Run jsonkit mcp <command> -h for command details.
